.TH ferry-network 1  Ferry "Ferry Manual"
.SH NAME
ferry\-network \- Show or change the network mode: `local` (no external servers, default), `internet` (also through the free public iroh relays, for devices in different networks), `relay` (also through your own relays) or `relay\-only` (only through your own relays, never directly)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBferry network\fR [\fB\-\-lang\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIMODE\fR] [\fIRELAYS\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Show or change the network mode: `local` (no external servers, default), `internet` (also through the free public iroh relays, for devices in different networks), `relay` (also through your own relays) or `relay\-only` (only through your own relays, never directly)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-lang\fR \fI<CODE>\fR
Interface language for this run (`en`, `pl`); overrides the saved setting
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fIMODE\fR]
Mode to save: `local`, `internet`, `relay` or `relay\-only`
.TP
[\fIRELAYS\fR]
With `relay` or `relay\-only`: the relay URLs (`https://relay.example.org`); without them the saved ones are kept
